  <prompt>Owner 2026-11-26: "Yes, start group C" (deferred-issue triage group C, notes/deferred-triage-2026-11.md). Two small Signals fixes; read gh issue view 1848 and gh issue view 1881. (1) #1848: DecisionActionCatalog.cs (Services/Signals/Actions), revise-budget parameter budget, Hint "Pre-selected when the matter has one budget; the user picks one when it has several (D-18)" is shown to users. Replace with copy addressed to the decider, e.g. "Chosen automatically when the matter has one budget; pick the budget to revise when it has several." Scan the catalog for any other (D-nn) or developer wording in user-visible strings and fix those too. The plan text is pinned in contract baselines (tests/integration/contract/Api/Signals/Baselines/plan.200.*.json): update them in the same PR. (2) #1881: SignalEvaluator.AssigneeColumnBySubject (SignalEvaluator.cs ~109) maps sprk_workassignment to sprk_assignedto; D-129 and OwnedChildWrite.ForPersonColumns name sprk_assignedtointernal. Take the column from ForPersonColumns["sprk_workassignment"].Column (or the same source), and add a test that pins the two maps together for every subject both define. Line numbers at origin/master d43fc9e16d.</prompt>
  <role>SPAARKE backend developer: .NET 10 BFF, the ontology Signals catalog and evaluator.</role>
  <goal>No user-visible catalog string carries a decision id or developer wording, and the evaluator and the worklist agree on who a work assignment's individual is.</goal>
  <context>
    <background>D-129: individuals come from Assigned To Internal (sprk_assignedtointernal), or sprk_assignedto1 on sprk_invoice/sprk_event; never ownerid. The pinning test should fail if the two maps diverge for a shared subject.</background>
  </context>
